@               Non-VXI Device Configuration Editor
               -----------------------------------
   
Use this editor to statically assign address space and interrupt lines
to non-VXI devices. The Resource Manager needs information about the
static attributes of the installed non-VXI devices in order to avoid
conflicts when it dynamically configures the VXI devices.

Field Description:
------------------
PseudoLA: Logical address of non-VXI device (0x100 and 0x1ff, hex)

Device Name: Device name, 12-character ASCII name

Frame: Logical address of frame extender (VXI-MXI) (hex)

Slot: Slot number (hex)

MfrId: Manufacturer number, 4 characters (hex)

Model Code: Model number, 4 characters (hex)

DevClass: 0 = Memory, 1 = Extended, 2 = Message-Based, 3 = Register-Based

Model Name: 12-character ASCII name

Mfr Name: Manufacturer name, 12-character ASCII name

a16membase: Base of A16 memory (hex)

a16memsize: Size of A16 memory (hex bytes)

a24membase: Base of A24 memory (hex)

a24memsize: Size of A24 memory (hex bytes)

a32membase: Base of A32 memory (hex)

a32memsize: Size of A32 memory (hex bytes)

Irq Level: Interrupt levels (bit vec, bits 0-6 for levels 1-7, hex)

IrqHandle: Interrupt Handlers (bit vec, bits 0-6 for levels 1-7, hex)

InSystem: If the device is presently in the system (0=no, 1=yes)

Usage
-----
This editor supports the following commands:

(1) list      [<index#>,[<index#>]] - lists all the entries in the 
                                      specified range.
(2) display   [<index#>,[<index#>]] - displays the entries in detail.
(3) add                             - lets you add an entry.
(4) duplicate  <index#>             - lets you duplicate an entry.
(5) modify     <index#>,<field#>    - lets you modify an existing entry.
(6) delete     <index#>             - lets you delete an entry.
(7) show       <field#>             - shows information about the field.
(8) save                            - lets you save the information.
(9) abort                           - lets you exit the editor, 
                                      ignoring the changes made.
(10) exit                           - lets you exit the editor.
(11) help                           - gives help on that editor.


@


